2026-07-31 16:28:25,601 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 1, 'text': 'B7 (CONFIRMED, out of scope for lib-camuart): the I2C camera path is dead hardware, not dead code.\nmain.cpp:41,496 (`#include <M5CameraSource.h>`, `static mtchunk::M5CameraSource g_cam`) and the\n`cam snap`/`cam refresh`/`cam read`/etc command handlers (~1945-2070) compile UNCONDITIONALLY --\nno `#ifdef CAM_I2C` or `#ifndef CAM_UART` guards anything. M5CameraSource.h (rak/lib/mt-chunk/src/,\nline 15) documents its wiring as camera SCL->RAK SCL (G13), SDA->RAK SDA (G4) -- physically\ndifferent pins from SERIAL_CAM\'s UART (pins 15/16). Per main.cpp:57-61\'s own comment, the camera\nmoved onto the UART pins in the 2026-07-21 rewire. So `g_cam.wake()`/`.capture()`/etc reach for an\nI2C device that has not been physically connected on those pins since that rewire -- the code\nbuilds and would run, it just addresses hardware that is not there. Distinct from B naming\ncollision risk: this is NOT the same finding as the earlier (pre-restructure) note about\nM5CameraSource "never compiling in the flashed env" -- it DOES compile in rak4631_camuart; it is\nUNREACHABLE FUNCTIONALLY, not at compile time. Found during lib-camuart re-investigation,\n2026-07-31. Not fixing -- out of scope for lib-camuart (which only touches the UART framing\nprotocol, not the I2C path or the `cam` command family).'}
