2026-07-31 16:30:15,583 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 1, 'text': 'B8 (CONFIRMED, out of scope for lib-camuart): comment contradicts code at main.cpp:607-618.\n`grep -n "#ifdef CAM_UART\\|#endif" main.cpp` shows the outer `#ifdef CAM_UART` opened at :528 does\nNOT close until :676 (a second, nested, redundant `#ifdef CAM_UART`/`#endif` pair sits inside it at\n:620/:639). So `g_camAlive` (:610) and the heap-history vars `g_heapMinFree`/`g_heapEmaPct`\n(:617-618) are INSIDE that guard, despite the comment directly above them claiming "Defined\nunconditionally so a non-camera build honestly reports cam:0 in status" (:608-609). If a\nnon-CAM_UART env is ever built, `g_camAlive` would not exist and any reference to it outside\n528-676 would fail to compile -- meaning either the claim is stale (no non-CAM_UART env has\nactually been built in a long time, so this was never exercised) or `g_camAlive` is referenced\nonly inside the guard elsewhere too (not checked further -- out of scope). Found during\nlib-camuart\'s spec-writing pass, 2026-07-31. Not fixing -- moving the 5 functions this task\nactually extracts (camCrc16/camuSend/camuRecv/camuPoll/camuFlush, :534-605) does not touch this\nregion or change this behavior either way.'}
