2026-07-31 16:30:34,095 1251 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 1, 'text': 'RE-INVESTIGATED 2026-07-31 (ownership blocker resolved -- esp32cam/ now git-tracked inside this\nrepo since the restructure, no longer cross-session). Confirmed:\n\nSCOPE for THIS extraction, narrowed from the original task title: only the 5 pure-framing\nfunctions, NOT camBootProbe/camGrabBegin (those belong to the future mt-camera lib per the\n2026-07-30 two-lib correction -- they touch grab-state/B5, a different concern):\n  camCrc16   main.cpp:534-543\n  camuSend   main.cpp:544-552\n  camuRecv   main.cpp:554-571\n  camuPoll   main.cpp:578-604 (incl. g_camuF/g_camuFLen/g_camuFGot/g_camuCrcGot/g_camuCrcB/g_camuSt state)\n  camuFlush  main.cpp:605\ncamCrc16 has no external callers (used only inside these 5) -- confirmed via grep, safe to make\nprivate. camuPoll\'s frame buffer (g_camuF) IS read directly by the caller (grab-state machine,\nmain.cpp ~3432-3493, future mt-camera territory) after a successful poll -- needs a public\naccessor in the new class, not just an internal detail.\n\nDUAL-PLATFORM CONFIRMED, not assumed: esp32cam/src/main.cpp:228-246 has its own independent\ncrc16()/uartSend() -- SAME CRC16-CCITT algorithm (poly 0x1021, seed 0xFFFF), same wire framing\n[7E][len][payload][crc16], written as separate, hand-duplicated code. Both boards run the Arduino\nframework (nordicnrf52 / espressif32) and both SERIAL_CAM (RAK, rak/include/io.h:38, ==Serial1)\nand Serial1 (ESP32) are Stream-derived, so a Stream&-based class is portable to both -- confirmed\nvia grep of both platformio.ini files (arduino framework both sides).\n\nSCOPING THIS EXTRACTION AS RAK-ONLY, ESP32 ADOPTION DEFERRED: per this session\'s own\none-change-per-measurement discipline, swapping BOTH boards\' implementations in one pass would\nconflate two acceptance measurements (RAK pure-move vs ESP32 behavioral change) and require\ncamera hardware at the bench for the ESP32 side. This slice: pure-move the RAK side into a\nlibrary.json declaring platforms:["nordicnrf52","espressif32"] (so it\'s READY for the ESP32 side\nto adopt), verified pure-move on RAK only (nm/size diff, same method as mt-status/mt-rails).\nPointing esp32cam/platformio.ini at the new lib and swapping its hand-rolled copy is a separate,\nlater task -- esp32cam doesn\'t even have lib_extra_dirs wired to rak/lib/ yet.\n\nBug ledger: B7 (dead I2C camera path, unrelated hardware) and B8 (main.cpp:607-618 comment\ncontradicts #ifdef nesting) both logged, out of scope, not touched by this extraction.'}
